# sweep-pp-gpu.steps -- the post-process chain (gamma, contrast, r_scale,
# FXAA, the native-resolution 2D, bloom, soft particles, the water warp and
# r_softemu) on demo1, castle4 and the Shadow of Tremor mod's egypt (#340 P4).
# Needs the retail data in <basedir>/data1 and the mod in <basedir>/sot.
#
# Since P4a-2 the chain runs under -gpu on SDL_GPU render targets
# (rg_target.c), so the check is GL's frames against the backend's, one
# binary both ways, with tools/pp-diff.sh:
#
#   A="-fsaa 0 +gamma 1 +map demo1"
#   STEPS=tools/sweep-pp-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/pp-gl ~/hexen2 $A
#   VK_ICD_FILENAMES=<lvp_icd json> STEPS=tools/sweep-pp-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E \
#       ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/pp-gpu ~/hexen2 -gpu +gpu_allow_software 1 +gpu_debug 1 $A
#   ./tools/pp-diff.sh /tmp/pp-gl /tmp/pp-gpu
#
# Between each REPORT-<x>-BEGIN and -END in /tmp/pp-gpu/qconsole.log
# (DEMO1, CASTLE4, EGYPT) gpu_unrouted counts 0 calls -- reset ahead of
# each section, so the count covers every shot state, bloom's gated draws
# included -- and the validation layers (+gpu_debug 1) log no "Validation
# Error".  REPORT-BOOT is the boot's own count, before anything is reset.
#
# A change to the GL side is still checked GL against GL, as P4a-1 did: the
# binary before it and the one after, AE 0 on every frame the binary
# repeats (./tools/shot-diff.sh /tmp/pp-old /tmp/pp-new), and once more
# with -fsaa 4 in A for PP_CreateFBO's MSAA branch.
#
# THE FRAMES.  01-08 the graveyard (sweep-world-gpu.steps' 01 camera): PP off,
# the identity chain (r_waterwarp 1 above water wakes the chain and changes
# nothing), gamma 0.7, gamma 0.85 with contrast 1.5, r_scale 0.5 and 0.75,
# FXAA, and the three together.  14 the graveyard at gamma 0.9 and 20 the
# same with bloom.  09 the pools (sweep-liquid-gpu.steps' 01, translucent
# water into the scene FBO) and 13 the same with r_oit 1, which under -gpu
# must equal 09 (OIT is P6, gated off: a removed gate loses the water).  12
# the console, drawn into the native FBO.  20-29 reach the code P4b-P4e
# route: bloom on the graveyard and the torch room, soft particles on
# testentity sprites flush with the west wall with post-process off (the fb0
# depth snapshot) and on (pp_fbo's), the water warp from under the water,
# and r_softemu 1/2/3.  10 castle4's lava and 11 egypt's north camera (the
# stencil in pp_fbo's depth texture) at gamma 0.9.  pp-diff.sh compares 01-14,
# 22-24 and 26-28 against GL, and 20 against 14 on -gpu (the bloom gate); 21
# and 25 are not compared (21 waits for P4e bloom).  22-24 joined at P4b
# (56.9 - 57.0 dB on its binary; tools/sweep-softpart-gpu.steps checks the
# fade itself).  The 3D-effects pass (PP_BlitWith3DEffects: the underwater
# warp, motion blur) is tools/sweep-warp-gpu.steps' since P4c, with
# r_pp_time holding the warp's phase.
#
# GAMMA BELOW 1 ONLY.  V_UpdatePalette (view.c) puts any gamma above 1 back
# to 1, so a "gamma 1.2" frame is the gamma-1 frame and proves nothing: the
# first P4a-2 runs had 14 (then gamma 1.2) equal to 01 on -gpu, and GL's
# differing only by the fault below.  Every gamma here is 0.7-0.9.
#
# 14 IS SHOT AFTER 20, with r_bloom back at 0: it is the check that a bloom
# frame leaves nothing behind.  The bloom upsample used to leave the blend
# func at GL_ONE, GL_ONE, so on GL the sky's front layer went additive for
# every frame from 20 to restart (sky mean 0.53 where 08's, at the same
# gamma, is 0.29), and 14 was shot first to keep out of it.  GitHub #547;
# tools/bloom-sky-check.sh.
#
# 25-underwater-warp is not repeatable: the warp's phase is realtime, which
# pause does not stop, and this sweep leaves r_pp_time at -1 so its frames
# stay comparable with the ones before P4c.  Compare it against the
# run-to-run spread of one binary, not against AE 0.
#
# Settings as sweep-liquid-gpu.steps, for the same reasons, plus
# con_notifytime 0: each `cmd` echoes into the notify lines at the top of the
# screen for three seconds of realtime, which made 02 differ from 01 in text,
# not in rendering.  pp-diff.sh masks the mini status bar's health
# (210x24+100+576: it reads 83 or 85 by run) and, in 12-console, the input
# cursor (20,273-30,283), which blinks on realtime (sweep-2d.steps' second
# trap).
#
# THE THRESHOLDS -- see tools/pp-diff.sh for the checks.  Measured
# 2026-11-24, 800x600, llvmpipe GL (Mesa 26.1.8) against lavapipe -gpu,
# three runs a side, two GL runs of master beside them, PSNR in dB, masked:
#
#   frames                       GL vs -gpu    GL vs GL    P4 vs GL      gate
#   01-08, 10, 11, 14            53.1 .. 82.0  inf         46.2 .. 58.0  42
#     (07 FXAA 53.1 and 08 FXAA + r_scale 54.6, FXAA's edge taps; the
#      rest 72.3 .. 82.0)
#   09, 13 the pools, 12 console 47.6 .. 47.9  47.6, 61.2  45.8 .. 48.4  42
#     (the water and the console's backdrop animate under pause: GL
#      against itself reads 47.6 on the pools, 61.2 on the console)
#   26-28 r_softemu              64.2 .. 66.5  inf         41.7 .. 42.2  40
#
# GL against GL is the same binary three times and master against it twice:
# every frame the binary repeats is identical, old against new included.
# "P4" is -gpu on the Tesla P4 (NVIDIA Vulkan) against the llvmpipe GL
# frames, one run: 0 validation errors, gpu_unrouted 0, every check passing
# but 26 and 27 at 42 (41.9, 41.7), where palette snapping turns the two
# rasterizers' last-bit differences (51-52 dB on 01 and 14) into whole
# palette steps -- hence the r_softemu frames' gate of 40, which r_softemu
# dropped (26-28 against 14, the same frame without it) misses by 2.4 dB
# or more: 35.1 .. 37.6.  The 42 gate is 5.6 dB under the worst honest
# lavapipe frame (the pools) and 11.1 under the worst static one.
#
# Broken builds, one -gpu run each (BRK=<proxy> in a scratch build, never
# committed), every one failing pp-diff.sh:
#
#   proxy      what it breaks                          worst check
#   bind       draw-framebuffer binds ignored          02-28 at 10.8 .. 17.6
#   noblit     End3D's colour blit claimed, not made   02-28 at 12.4 .. 19.3,
#                                                      2x2 blocks, both gates
#   flip       the colour blit flips rows              02-28 at 15.3 .. 20.7
#   sampler    the final pass's scene sampler unset    02-28 at 0.8 .. 2.3
#   noflush    PpParams never flushed                  02-28 at 10.8 .. 17.6
#   firstall   every target's first pass clears        02-28 at 4.8 .. 11.1
#   oit        the OIT gates removed (P6)              13 at 24.7, oit gate,
#                                                      4282 null-table calls
#   bloom      the bloom gate removed (P4e)            bloom gate (89812 px)
#   fbofail    every framebuffer incomplete            03-28 at 19.2 .. 38.8,
#                                                      every effect check
#   nostencil  pp_fbo's depth without stencil          11 at 16.5
#
# Two proxies pass and say why: "viewport" (End3D's native R_SetViewport
# left out) is redundant, since GL_SetCanvas sets the 2D's viewport anyway;
# "noclear" (new render targets never cleared) draws the same frames on
# lavapipe and on the Tesla P4, pixel for pixel against the honest P4 run
# outside the animated pools and console: the chain clears or overwrites
# all of pp_fbo and pp_native_fbo before it reads them, so the creation
# clear guards a target read before anything wrote it, which no frame here
# does.

sleep 20
cmd echo REPORT-BOOT-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd echo REPORT-BOOT-END
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd noclip
cmd con_notifytime 0
cmd viewsize 120
cmd crosshair 0
cmd showpause 0
cmd r_skyspeed_back 0
cmd r_skyspeed_front 0
cmd r_flatlightstyles 1
cmd r_dynamic 0
cmd r_gpulightstyles 0
cmd r_ssao 0
cmd r_bloom 0
cmd r_dlight_occlusion 0
cmd r_alias_gpu 0
cmd r_particles 0
cmd fog 0
cmd gl_texture_anisotropy 1
cmd r_oit 0
cmd r_waterwarp 0
cmd r_motionblur 0
cmd r_softparticles 0
cmd r_softemu 0
cmd r_scale 1
cmd gl_fxaa 0
cmd contrast 1
cmd gl_waterwarp_speed 0
cmd r_caustics 0
cmd gl_glows 0
cmd r_drawviewmodel 0
cmd r_drawentities 0
cmd r_wateralpha 0.33
cmd r_lavaalpha 0
cmd r_water_pixel_warp 0
sleep 2

# --- the graveyard: the chain core ---
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 -20 45 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 01-gy-ppoff
cmd r_waterwarp 1
shot 02-gy-identity
cmd r_waterwarp 0
cmd gamma 0.7
shot 03-gy-gamma07
cmd gamma 0.85
cmd contrast 1.5
shot 04-gy-g085-c15
cmd gamma 1
cmd contrast 1
cmd r_scale 0.5
shot 05-gy-scale050
cmd r_scale 0.75
shot 06-gy-scale075
cmd r_scale 1
cmd gl_fxaa 1
shot 07-gy-fxaa
cmd gamma 0.9
cmd r_scale 0.5
shot 08-gy-combo
cmd r_scale 1
cmd gl_fxaa 0
cmd r_softemu 1
shot 26-gy-softemu1
cmd r_softemu 2
shot 27-gy-softemu2
cmd r_softemu 3
shot 28-gy-softemu3
cmd r_softemu 0
cmd r_bloom 1
cmd r_bloom_threshold 0.5
shot 20-gy-bloom
cmd r_bloom 0
cmd r_bloom_threshold 1
shot 14-gy-gamma09
cmd gamma 1
cmd pause

# --- the pools, translucent water into the scene FBO; then r_oit 1 ---
cmd setpos -1007 2200 -442 25 152 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
cmd gamma 0.9
shot 09-pools
cmd r_oit 1
shot 13-pools-oit
cmd r_oit 0
cmd gamma 1
cmd pause

# --- 2D into the native FBO: the console over the pools ---
# Cleared first: the boot log above it differs by backend (the -gpu lines,
# the bloom pyramid's DPrintfs on GL), and that is text, not rendering.
cmd clear
cmd gamma 0.9
console
sleep 1
shot 12-console
console
sleep 1
cmd gamma 1

# --- soft particles on sprites by the graveyard's west wall ---
cmd r_drawentities 1
cmd testentity models/bldspot1.spr -1320 -1640 60 0 180 0
cmd testentity models/s_light.spr -1250 -1770 60
cmd testentity models/s_light.spr -1318 -1700 40
cmd testentity models/s_explod.spr -1270 -1850 40 0 0 0 3 128
cmd setpos -1150 -1800 0 0 170 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 24-sprites-hard
cmd r_softparticles 1
shot 22-sprites-soft-ppoff
cmd gamma 0.9
shot 23-sprites-soft-pp
cmd r_softparticles 0
cmd gamma 1
cmd pause
cmd r_drawentities 0

# --- bloom in the torch room ---
cmd setpos -1536 1900 -450 0 90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
cmd gl_glows 1
cmd r_bloom 1
cmd r_bloom_threshold 0.5
shot 21-torch-bloom
cmd r_bloom 0
cmd r_bloom_threshold 1
cmd gl_glows 0
cmd pause

# --- the water warp, from under the water (not repeatable, see above) ---
cmd setpos -2000 1600 -520 -50 90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
cmd r_waterwarp 1
shot 25-underwater-warp
cmd r_waterwarp 0
cmd pause

# --- report: the demo1 shot states once more, counted ---
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 -20 45 0
cmd gamma 0.9
cmd gl_fxaa 1
cmd r_scale 0.5
sleep 2
cmd r_scale 1
cmd gl_fxaa 0
cmd r_softparticles 1
cmd r_oit 1
sleep 2
cmd r_oit 0
cmd r_softparticles 0
cmd gamma 1
sleep 1
cmd echo REPORT-DEMO1-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd renderer_status
cmd echo REPORT-DEMO1-END
sleep 1

# --- castle4: the lava pit ---
console
enter map castle4
sleep 20
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd noclip
cmd setpos 1652 1496 -646 20 88 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
cmd gamma 0.9
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
shot 10-c4-lava
cmd echo REPORT-CASTLE4-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd echo REPORT-CASTLE4-END
cmd gamma 1
cmd pause

# --- egypt (the Shadow of Tremor mod): the stencilled skybox in pp_fbo ---
# The game switch re-execs the mod's own config and autoexec, so every
# setting above is set again after it.
cmd game sot
sleep 60
console
sleep 2
console
enter map egypt
sleep 45
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd noclip
cmd con_notifytime 0
cmd viewsize 120
cmd crosshair 0
cmd showpause 0
cmd r_skyspeed_back 0
cmd r_skyspeed_front 0
cmd r_skybox_speed 0
cmd r_flatlightstyles 1
cmd r_dynamic 0
cmd r_gpulightstyles 0
cmd r_ssao 0
cmd r_bloom 0
cmd r_dlight_occlusion 0
cmd r_alias_gpu 0
cmd r_particles 0
cmd fog 0
cmd gl_texture_anisotropy 1
cmd r_oit 0
cmd r_waterwarp 0
cmd r_motionblur 0
cmd r_softparticles 0
cmd r_softemu 0
cmd r_scale 1
cmd gl_fxaa 0
cmd contrast 1
cmd gl_waterwarp_speed 0
cmd r_caustics 0
cmd gl_glows 0
cmd r_drawviewmodel 0
cmd r_drawentities 0
sleep 2
cmd setpos 784 1760 236 -40 180 0
sleep 3
cmd setpos 784 1760 236 -40 180 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
cmd gamma 0.9
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
shot 11-egypt-north
cmd echo REPORT-EGYPT-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd echo REPORT-EGYPT-END
cmd gamma 1
cmd pause
sleep 1
